Z||000011||Tina||04-04-2001||11:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Tina,<P>yep the rate I got for dells is $72 a night, is that the right rate? that show is right before my finals, but ah thats ok, its just studying   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Single or double occupancy?<BR>Just looked at my Reservation at Chula Vista<P>Paid $90 for double occupancy per night with<BR>Fiero Fanatic discount applied.<BR>Otherwise it would have been like $150 for the same room.<P>Just in case you need it.<BR>Their # is #1-800-388-4782 or <A HREF="http://www.chulavistaresort.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chulavistaresort.com</A> <P>See ya there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||RossT||04-05-2001||12:12 AM||||My Dells Run reservations also came too 90 dollars a night with taxes added in.  We have a room overlooking the car show with a balcony. Nothing like waking up in the morning and looking out your window to see 140+ fieros!!!<P>The 80-90 dollar rooms are in the main tower, while there are cheaper rooms not in the tower. <P>The hotel is about full, so if you want a room, make your reservations now!!<P>Tina, look forward to seeing you there!  Will you have a v-8 stuffed into that blue t-top in time???||||reg||1
Z||000013||Archie||04-05-2001||08:05 AM||||I made my reservations in the Dells yesterday AM. According to the guy who I talked to, they still have plenty of rooms for that weekend. They do expect reservations to start pouring in right after Easter though, you might want to reserve your room(s) pretty soon then.<P>You may want to note that reservations made now can still be cancelled 3 days before the event without charge. Because of this there are always rooms that "Open up" just a day or 2 before the show. I have 3 Suites reserved in the main Tower this time.  This year, I figure that I'd rather be one of the people who release an extra room to late comers that be waiting for one to open up. <P>Archie ||||reg||1
Z||000014||kslish||04-05-2001||08:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>if anyone wants to pack in a room, let me know.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm, might be an interesting project..."just how many Fiero fanatics can you pack into a room?"  Might make a Guiness World Record or something.<P>On a more serious note Lisa, I'll be in touch about the Nationals or maybe Michigan if you have room (not planning on attending Dells).  <P>The cost of the rooms really suck when I think about the fact that I really don't spend that much time in a room at all when I attend these shows, just too much to get out and see.<P>I'm also seriously considering a room for Carlisle this year for at least one night.  Not sure if I feel like catching some Z's in a Turnpike rest stop again like last year.  You and Chris would be welcome if he is attending (provided I get to drive his Northstar, he-he).<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||mrfixit58||04-05-2001||10:13 AM||||Oh, ME, ME  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> !!! Uh-Oh, the wife said: "You mean the pretty girl in the bikini? NO WAY!". Huh... who'd a thunk it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">??<P>Have fun anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000016||RossT||04-05-2001||11:15 AM||||This is from the Wisconsin Fiero web page about the Dells Run:<P>"Dells 2001 Updates<P>Invitations are in the mail to the Original 22 Fiero Owners that attended our 1992 Dells Run, we want them to come back and see just how much this event has changed in 10 years.  We are looking for volunteers to help at this years event, call the hot-line at (414) 282-3577 and leave your name and number, I will call you back with more information on what we need done.  I am looking for someone in the club that can make picture frames so we can show off the dells shirts that we have made for the last ten years.  If you can do this, give me a call, we only have to do 10 of them, but I'm no good at getting them to stay together.  This years event will have a few changes that should surprise everyone, more cruises, Fiero Bingo, dancing, eating and the wildest car show of the year.   $100.00 for the best in each class, $50.00 for the best model car, Free Weekend at Chula Vista for some lucky winner.  The list goes on and on.  Tell your friends, neighbors and country men, this is the Best in the Mid-West for Fiero Fun.<P>I've been in contact with Chula-Vista and the rooms are going at a faster rate than any other year.  Out buildings are gone, parking lot side of tower is gone!  They are filling fast and we are looking into SPILLOVER HOTELS!!!  Call now or you will be left out.  I have entries from 10 states already and I have no idea how many people will be there.  The internet is a buzz with everyone talking about 2001 Dells Run.   I think we will be breaking records this year.<P>The Fanatics will be doing the Greenfield 4th of July Parade, then cruise to Jessica's for malts and burgers.  This is always a great time to do everything with your family and friends.  Parade is at 8:00 a.m.<P>Remember, now is the time to mail in your car show information.  It takes time to put together an event.  Our spring tune up tour is on May 6th.  The Fanatics will be doing another first, having our Fieros Blessed!  You don't want to miss this one.  <P>BREAKING NEWS...The Illinois Chapter will raffle off 1988 T-Top at Fierorama!  $10.00 a chance.  More info as soon as it is made available"<P><BR>It could be that they are trying to get everyone to book early!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||FieroLisa||04-05-2001||11:22 AM||||Ken- right now have 4 people in the room at Natl's which gets the cost down to about 23 bucks a person per night. So if someone really doesn't mind being smooshed they can stay ,but that room is pretty much full ( we can't have the hotel knowing theres more than one person in there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> As for Michigan, right now there's just me and Chris in the room right now, so there's space. Just email me and let me know your plans!||||reg||1
